	description: 'Implement the retrying and blocked states from tasks/j1/states.md (section Failures) with the user decisions there: temporary failures retry at once then back off and never give up on their own; 429 and quota rotate to the next account for the same model (reference: the old account-rotation.ts, artifact) and otherwise wait for the provider-given time, surviving restart; broken auth blocks on login and continues by itself once the credentials file works again (it is a live file); bad requests end the turn in error with the provider message, and continue retries. Laptop sleep must be invisible to the user: this is the one place where defensive, hard-to-test code is allowed. Detect wake with an injected clock (timer gap), treat streams open across it as dropped, and say in comments which failure each guard is for. Every state names its time or reason in snapshots so clients show "retrying in 12s (connection lost)" or "blocked: log in".',
